-- title:
--   Smoothness of the resolved model off the edge points
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak X$ be a [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage p`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackage.html#L43), i.e. the two-chart integral Deligne–Rapoport model over $\mathbb Z$ together with its properness, flatness, integrality and normality data, the curve models of its fibres over $\mathbb Q$ and over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with their Galois and place compatibilities, the two cuspidal sections, and its smooth-locus open. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $H$ be a collection [`V3Asm.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L267) of hypotheses for this site datum: finiteness of the node set $\mathrm{Node}\,p\,\mathfrak X\,\kappa$ (the fibre product of the two components $\mathfrak X$.compInf and $\mathfrak X$.compZero over $\kappa$), existence of oriented crossing charts, étale-neighbourhood data, injectivity of the assignment of node points and closedness of each of them, and the model hypotheses. Assume moreover that each point $\xi_j$ lies in the open `X0` of the chart input $C$, the complement of the finitely many marked node points. Then there is an open subscheme $W$ of the glued scheme $Y$ obtained from this resolution datum such that the inclusion of $W$ followed by the structure morphism $Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$, and such that every point $y$ of $Y$ which is distinct from all the edge points $\mathrm{edgePt}(n,d)$, for $n$ a node and $d < \mathrm{width}(n)$ (the thickness of the chart input at $n$), belongs to $W$.
--
--   This records, for the glued resolution of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ over a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$, that the resolved model is smooth of relative dimension one away from the finitely many edge points of the resolution chains sitting over the crossings. It is used in the assembly of the resolved model package together with its étale crossing charts.
